#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128983 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "5110af12-1d0a-5f7e-8a3b-626cc437c53e" :question/math-academy-id "e-6097" :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{4}  \\int_{0}^{2} \\dfrac{x^3}{y^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x  \\, \\textrm{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{4}}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4{[-\\frac{1}{y}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{4}-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128984 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/id #uuid "bd93891e-1f9f-51af-a5c2-4eb5ca1178d9" :question/math-academy-id "e-6098" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} \\dfrac y{x^2} \\, \\textrm d A$, where \n$D=\\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\:2 \\leq x \\leq 4,\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 3\\right\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[-\\frac{y}{x}]}_{2}^{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-\\frac{y}{4}-(-\\frac{y}{2}))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128985 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/id #uuid "e51c2aa9-027b-5b23-bcaf-805804a8de9c" :question/math-academy-id "e-6099" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}.$\n\nI. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}y \\, \\text{d}x$\n\nII. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{2}  \\int_{0}^{1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}y\\,  \\text{d}x$\n\nIII. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}x \\, \\text{d}y$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that: \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from ${\\color{blue}0}$ to ${\\color{blue}2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from ${\\color{red}0}$ to ${\\color{red}1}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  \n= \\int_{\\color{blue}0}^{\\color{blue}{2}} \\left[ \\int_{\\color{red}0}^{\\color{red}1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}{\\color{red}y} \\right] \\text{d}{\\color{blue}x} .\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "907234f6-d41d-59c4-b707-3a4bc0a94e07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128540} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ed8dda-c357-5308-97b6-a92c738ce5dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128541} {:answer/id #uuid "f9741cfe-9a2e-51ba-9f5d-1bbc05258f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128542} {:answer/id #uuid "0b435149-51ff-523f-b255-3bdd5a506e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128543} {:answer/id #uuid "704224b1-5570-5b35-8983-4889e11c0891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b435149-51ff-523f-b255-3bdd5a506e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128543} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b810ea7-b064-5fb2-907f-f94838c98873" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd6a034f-87ae-5507-9abe-98641b443d7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-71930" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$\n\nI. ${∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nII. ${∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that:\n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $1$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $1$ to $3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f04548b-c5b2-5dd6-91f7-ac226f8ce5f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443724} {:answer/id #uuid "6c9577fe-e0ea-5924-a5a3-56d0d5cd71b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443725} {:answer/id #uuid "be4791cb-b433-5220-a3ae-6b3c2cac9bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443726} {:answer/id #uuid "dec4c0cb-7929-5b16-9e0e-753322768bf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443727} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ea7f02-d0bc-58f0-b333-df298335e3ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8ea7f02-d0bc-58f0-b333-df298335e3ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443728} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe184e8e-6c3d-5fe7-aa56-1a1728b67c6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1fae684a-7e13-519a-aef1-3caa737a3e69" :question/math-academy-id "q-72178" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,-1\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{3}\\}.$\n\nI. ${∬}_{D}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1/3}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nII. ${∬}_{D}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1/3}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1}^{1/3}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that:      \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $-\\frac{1}{2}$ to $\\frac{1}{2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-1$ to $\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1/3}[{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can also swap the order of integration. This gives \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}[{\\int }_{-1}^{1/3}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3906178d-d2b9-5c1e-8874-62464ff4587d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336568} {:answer/id #uuid "485ed612-6290-5d86-b376-ce0eb70b3fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336705} {:answer/id #uuid "51a463d3-0093-55d7-a2ee-8312594e1a86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336780} {:answer/id #uuid "87045c5e-f1ca-5e3e-850f-ac86db303947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337253} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea3d299-fb71-5298-b534-c642be602e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "485ed612-6290-5d86-b376-ce0eb70b3fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336705} :answer-field/id #uuid "1eab19eb-a5c0-56fa-880c-7541dcfdcaf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2290a5a5-423d-532e-a1cb-06c374bf7c6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-72268" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y(1-0)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =-2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-2\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382263 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "824359cf-f8f4-52d6-ba3e-38e5e3b7039d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382265} {:answer/id #uuid "5d49b3c7-4f50-56c5-914d-a87761849f4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382266} {:answer/id #uuid "49e46a24-677b-55ca-84d4-a49ee89da34b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382267} {:answer/id #uuid "dc529383-f4e5-5451-b49b-b79fd5352caf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382268} {:answer/id #uuid "adcc0123-a959-56a4-8c2a-3f66fbcf1437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc529383-f4e5-5451-b49b-b79fd5352caf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382268} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdb31333-a57a-513c-a580-7da1020dfc71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0386666-3fac-5a95-aad2-f27d650f7552" :question/math-academy-id "q-73576" :question/problem "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+2y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}[{\\int }_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+2y)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+2y)]_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+\\frac{5\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+\\pi ))\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12} & (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+\\frac{5\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+\\pi ))\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y+\\frac{5\\pi }{3})+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y+\\pi )]}_{0}^{\\pi /12} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{5\\pi }{3})+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0+\\frac{5\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & +\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0+\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{6})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}-0] \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342021 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23119422-3823-57bd-ae60-3a70da203882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339428} {:answer/id #uuid "3233eb3a-80c4-5e2c-afa0-25c63262aae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339569} {:answer/id #uuid "8c653da2-7477-595d-a51e-c3f66f8b5ff3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340387} {:answer/id #uuid "cce2e1a4-aa36-57b6-badd-2c432cb8566b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340942} {:answer/id #uuid "e95bda4b-27fc-570d-96c8-8ec990cd3092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cce2e1a4-aa36-57b6-badd-2c432cb8566b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340942} :answer-field/id #uuid "738ace53-c45e-5df6-a139-2497bca10161" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d286237-0b02-5319-9c6e-7aa25af2bd91" :question/math-academy-id "q-73583" :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral\n${\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}{\\int }_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}(1+9{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}[{\\int }_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}(1+9{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{3}{(1+(3x)^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)]_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1))\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{\\pi }{12{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{\\pi }{12{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[-\\frac{\\pi }{12y}]}_{1/3}^{1/4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}}+\\frac{\\pi }{12\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382270 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c27e5d9e-ecc8-5521-979e-959ae11dfb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382272} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf8410f-256c-5c3a-88a9-1e54c1305a5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382273} {:answer/id #uuid "1f8b2ae9-6d97-53ea-9139-300db65317f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382274} {:answer/id #uuid "c8e57571-1b7b-56fa-89dc-50c902f9aaa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382275} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e3852e-29df-51ea-a355-6527795c1a18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8e57571-1b7b-56fa-89dc-50c902f9aaa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382275} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a37391c-0888-5ae0-8a15-f1ed7e46bd73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6487b6b9-d5be-5e16-b654-46f92252f451" :question/math-academy-id "q-73586" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,-3\\le y\\le -1\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:      \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{3}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}\\frac{9}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}\\frac{9}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y & =9{[-\\frac{1}{2{y}^{2}}]}_{-3}^{-1} \\\\  & =9(-\\frac{1}{2(-1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2(-3)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
